References (no code copied — wire format / spec / convention only)
================================================================================

The following projects influenced Akagi v3 by their public protocols, wire
formats, or conventions, but no source code was copied from them. They are
listed here for credit only.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MajsoulMax-rs
  https://github.com/Xerxes-2/MajsoulMax-rs
  Licensed under GPL-3.0.

  Used as a reference for the 5-layer Majsoul WebSocket wire format
  (type byte -> Wrapper -> inner message -> action protobuf) in
  src/proxy/handler.rs, src/bridge/majsoul/parser.rs, and
  src/bridge/majsoul/proto/liqi.proto. Wire format only; no code copied.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mjai JSONL specification (Gimite)
  https://gimite.net/pukiwiki/index.php?Mjai

  Used to define the MjaiEvent enum and bot wire contract in src/schema/mjai/.
  Specification only.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mjai.app
  https://github.com/smly/mjai.app

  Subprocess convention reference (JSONL stdin/stdout, argv, env vars,
  end-of-batch flush) in src/bot/ and mjai_bot/. Convention only.

AkagiPlus modifications (2026-11-05): opt-in process-isolated MajsoulMax integration,
Cosmetics UI, source launchers, independent runtime data, and update isolation.
The bundled MajsoulMax-derived Python implementation is GPL-3.0; see
plugins/majsoulmax/PROVENANCE.md and plugins/majsoulmax/LICENSE.txt.

RiichiCity integration (2026):
- RiichiCityUnlock is an external user-provided program from https://github.com/Avenshy/RiichiCityUnlock ; no binary or proprietary source is redistributed.
- vendor/hudsucker is hudsucker 0.24.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0), with a local WebSocket CONNECT patch documented there. Original license files retained.

Amatsuki native capture (2026):
- plugins/amatsuki is an original read-only adapter. The IL2CPP reflection helper is shared from btlstar/AmatsukiStyle under Apache-2.0.
- Frida Python bindings 17.26.2: https://github.com/frida/frida-python ; wxWindows Library Licence 3.1, see LICENSES/frida-COPYING.txt.

AmatsukiStyle integration (2026):
- plugins/amatsukistyle includes the original AmatsukiStyle local cosmetic adapter, Apache-2.0; see its LICENSE.txt and NOTICE.
- Catalog parsing reads the user-installed game files; game assets and account profiles are not distributed.

RiichiCityStyle integration (2026):
- plugins/riichicity_local is the integrated RiichiCityStyle cosmetic core, Apache-2.0.
- Standalone manager: https://github.com/btlstar/RiichiCityStyle . Compatibility identifiers and existing local preferences are preserved.
